{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact head 989fd8297cadb34961930fc0a0b94ed5bdb6741a, under Hugh's c26ab49f request and Claude's 3f39121a promise. The sixteen candidate artifacts were reviewed, with cmd/gs/land.go first.\n\n1. HIGH — land.go:305 deletes an unmeasured remote tip. cleanupCandidate proves only that the approved candidate reached the target, finds a local branch pointing at that candidate, then runs git push origin --delete \u003cbranch\u003e. The remote branch can already contain newer unmerged work. An independent end-to-end fixture pushed a child commit only to origin's feature ref, landed the approved parent, and observed --cleanup remove that remote ref. Preserve an advanced remote tip and use an explicit expected-old lease for remote deletion; local deletion must likewise not force-delete a tip that moved after measurement. Cover remote divergence and movement during cleanup.\n\n2. MEDIUM — work_next.go:284 interpolates actor names into copyable shell commands without quoting. Actor provisioning permits spaces and shell metacharacters (app.go:976 rejects only slash, backslash, NUL and line breaks). With the valid name 'build bot', the printed command passes only 'build' to --as; shell metacharacters can instead become executable syntax when copied. Quote data arguments for the documented shell, keeping placeholders clearly distinguishable. An independent shell-token test reproduced the split.\n\n3. MEDIUM — work_next.go:265 emits gs inspect --as \u003cactor\u003e \u003cassert\u003e, but inspectCommand has no --as flag. Every such next command refuses with 'flag provided but not defined: -as'. Select flags appropriate to each subcommand and exercise the generated assertion-inspection line through its parser, not just a string assertion.\n\n4. MEDIUM — promise.go:78 only recognizes the initial claim's retry key. After withdrawal and a new successful claim, repeating the exact command refuses 'you already hold promise' rather than replay